    {
      "version": "0.7.1",
      "channel": "stable",
      "date": "2026-10-24",
      "status": "available",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/DreamWeave-MP/openmw-workbench",
        "tag": "openmw_workbench-0.7.1",
        "revision": "3cd3179fbdcdbb2e9a7766abfdf4a45c71f33e69"
      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "`self.ATTACK_TYPE` and nearby's enum tables are public API, and the contract that says so is generated from OpenMW's source.",
        "added": [
          "`tools/contract.jsl` writes `src/contract.jsl` from an OpenMW source tree: the Lua API spec, the C++ that installs packages and engine handlers, the builtin manifests, and the builtin Lua. The contract had no generator; this one reproduces it, and lists as engine-internal only the members the review's own reading can meet."
        ],
        "fixed": [
          "`self.ATTACK_TYPE`, `nearby.NAVIGATOR_FLAGS`, `nearby.COLLISION_SHAPE_TYPE` and `nearby.FIND_PATH_STATUS` are members, not engine-internal: the spec declares them as types without a field attaching them, and the C++ installs each on its package by that name. A review no longer warns that using them leans on undocumented API."
        ]
      },
